{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The excess is established on this trip's own measurement. The trace length is 22.5 km against a booked optimal of 18.0 km, an excess of 4.5 km and 25.00% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass: the excess exceeds 0.8 km in absolute terms and exceeds 20% of optimal. Under POL-RD-01 the governing field is gps_trace.trace_distance_km, and here the rounded trip_record copy (22.5 km) agrees with it, so the threshold is met on either figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02808", "EV-TRIP-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is clean, and POL-RD-07 cannot be used to dilute it. It carries 177 fixes at a 10 second sample interval against a 10 second expected interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps and a max_gap_sec of 0.0. None of POL-RD-07 limbs (a) to (c) fires, so the deviation may stand on the gps_trace alone, no independent corroboration under POL-RD-07(ii) is required, and the mandatory escalation in POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. The admissibility pre-pass agrees: EV-GPS-02808 is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's traffic advisory does not exonerate him, because POL-RD-03 requires all three of its limbs. Limb (c) demands an actual route that leaves the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoins it after. The record's own geometry check on the trace shows the vehicle's closest approach to the advisory area is 1,203.39 m, with 0 fixes inside that area and trace_enters_area false. A route that never comes within 1.2 km of the affected area did not route around it, so limb (c) fails and POL-RD-03 is unavailable. The advisory artifact's own note records that this check is the closest available test of limb (c) on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02808", "EV-ADVIS-02808-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.minimum_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (a) of POL-RD-03 is likewise not made out on the record, and the burden is the driver's. The advisory names the PIE towards Tuas after Eunos Link, but the optimal route's polyline is not in the record, so nothing establishes that the optimal route traverses the affected segment as limb (a) requires. The rider has already discharged his side under POL-RD-08: the trip identifiers and pickup timing match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and the threshold excess is shown on an unimpaired trace. The driver must then point to a specific artifact and a specific clause that excuses the excess; an untested assertion of 'accident on the PIE' does not discharge that burden. The advisory's window (06:09:18 to 07:33:38) does overlap the trip (06:39:18 to 07:08:38) so limb (b) is met, but all three limbs are conjunctive and two of them are not.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02808-01", "EV-TRIP-02808", "EV-GPS-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even taken at its highest, the advisory's own figures do not fit the drive. The advisory records the shortest lawful alternative over the booked endpoints as 21.0 km, yet the driver's trace runs 22.5 km - 1.5 km longer than the alternative the driver says he took, and 4.5 km longer than the booked optimal. That comparison is arithmetic on the record and is at least consistent with the vehicle not having followed the alternative the advisory documents, which is further reason to find limb (c) unsatisfied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02808-01", "EV-GPS-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the chat_log shifts any part of the excess to the rider. POL-RD-04 requires a rider instruction recorded in the chat_log that identifies an actionable place or road and is corroborated by the trace. The trip carries exactly one message, sent by the DRIVER at 06:40:48 - 'accident on the PIE ahead, taking the alternative' - with waypoint_hint null. There is no rider instruction at all, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable, no distance is excluded, and the driver's own route choice cannot be billed to the rider as if the rider had asked for it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline has not moved. POL-RD-05 requires an amended pickup or dropoff with a stored amended optimal. On this trip pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so no re-quote exists, the clause cannot be run, and the comparison point remains the booked optimal of 18.0 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No part of the 4.5 km excess is attributable to a co-rider. The vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-12 does not apply and the matched-itinerary baseline it substitutes for is not in play. The baseline is trip_record.optimal_distance_km of 18.0 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The distance-and-time refund route is open, because the fare model is metered. The fare breakdown records fare_model METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 (upfront-quoted fares) does not apply and no prepaid loss argument arises. POL-RD-02 governs the remedy, which is arithmetic and not discretionary.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund follows from the policy constants. On the booked optimal route: (3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.0 optimal km + 0.28 x 24.0 optimal min) = 24.02, multiplied by the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 24.02, plus the 0.80 platform fee, no ERP or tolls on the optimal route, no fixed surcharge, no waiting time fee and no promo discount = a recomputed_fare of 24.8200. Charged_total is 29.68. Refund = 29.68 - 24.82 = 4.86, which is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and only 16.37% of charged_total, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND and the payable figure rounds UP to SGD 4.90. The fare artifact's own refund block records the same unrounded 4.8600 and payable 4.90.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02808", "EV-TRIP-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The zero-refund scenario carried on the fare artifact does not decide anything, because it presupposes the exoneration the trace denies. That closure block reaches a recomputed fare of 29.8750 by setting justified_excess_km to 4.5 - the whole measured excess - and an adjusted optimal of 22.5 km, i.e. by assuming POL-RD-03 applies and excusing the entire deviation. Its intersects_route flag is an input to that scenario, not a finding that limb (c)'s corridor-leaving-and-rejoining test is met, and POL-RD-03 exonerates only where all three limbs hold. Strip out the exoneration and the arithmetic on the booked optimal is the 24.82 / 4.86 / 4.90 figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02808", "EV-GPS-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This record should be ruled on, not escalated. The trace's measured geometry and the fare artifact's closure scenario are not mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength under POL-RD-10(7): the geometry check is measured from a 100%-coverage trace at weight 1.0, while the closure block is arithmetic that is conditional on an exoneration the same trace contradicts. No other POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers all match, the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), the timestamps run forward and agree, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact, the computed refund of 4.86 is far below SGD 150.00 and below charged_total, and every charge line has its counterpart on the record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02808", "EV-FARE-02808", "EV-TRIP-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through line to add or to net off. The fare breakdown charges no ERP or toll (the erp_lines are empty, total 0.00) and no airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates at an airport nor is billed one, so POL-RD-09 produces no separate ERP correction here - and critically no off-route ERP to be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, which already comprehends only on-optimal-route gantries.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not overreach, and says so. The 4.5 km / 25% excess sits below the POL-RD-01 materiality line of 8.0 km and 50%, and the driver's profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 against completed_trips_90d of 399, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established on the only fields POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 permit for that test. The rider therefore claims the POL-RD-02 partial refund of SGD 4.90 and not a refund of the full 29.68 charged, and relies on no rating, account age, lifetime counter or prior-disputes field, all of which POL-GEN-01 makes context only.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02808", "EV-TRIP-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome the rider seeks is a rider win on the record as it stands. The rider filed this dispute, the payment status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.0, so NO_ACTION would leave the 29.68 charge in place and the rider carrying the disputed amount. PARTIAL_REFUND returns the 4.90 of unjustified distance and time to the rider, which is the only outcome on these numbers that relieves the rider of the disputed charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02808"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The deviation itself is real: trip TRP-02808 ran 22.5 km (EV-GPS-02808 trace_distance_km, and the trip record's rounded copy agrees) against a booked optimal of 18.0 km (EV-TRIP-02808), an excess of 4.5 km and 25.0% — over the POL-RD-01 thresholds of 0.8 km and 20%. The rider has proved that much. But POL-RD-03 exonerates the driver, so no refund follows and the SGD 29.68 charge stands. Why: an LTA DataMall advisory for this trip (EV-ADVIS-02808-01, ADV-20260818-055) records a HIGH-severity multi-vehicle accident blocking 2 of 3 lanes on the Pan Island Expressway towards Tuas after the Eunos Link exit, active 06:09:18–07:33:38 on 18 August 2026. It names a road the record marks as intersecting the trip's route (limb (a)), and its window covers the trip's 06:39:18–07:08:38 window with far more than the 15-minute buffer each end (limb (b)). Limb (c) is met on the record: the trace is unimpaired (177 fixes, 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, weight 1.0) and it records zero fixes inside the advisory area with a closest approach of 1,203.4 m, i.e. the vehicle did not drive the affected segment — so the actual route left the optimal corridor around that segment and rejoined it after, which is what limb (c) asks. The driver's in-app message of 06:40:48, inside the trip window, 'accident on the PIE ahead, taking the alternative', says the same thing contemporaneously. I have read the rider's contrary arguments and reject them: limb (c) does not require a route to pass close to the affected segment, and a route that stays out of it satisfies the limb rather than failing it; limb (a) is not undone by the missing optimal polyline, because the advisory names the road and the record marks it as intersecting the route; and the fact that the trace is 1.5 km longer than the shortest lawful alternative (21.0 km) does not defeat exoneration, because POL-RD-03's cap expressly tolerates it. The cap: justified excess = min(4.5, 1.30 x (21.0 - 18.0) + 1.00) = min(4.5, 4.90) = 4.5 km, so the whole measured excess is justified. On the closure-adjusted optimal of 22.5 km with a scaled duration of 30.0 min, the recomputed fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 22.5 + 0.28 x 30.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 29.8750, against a charged total of 29.68 (EV-FARE-02808) — a refund floored at zero. The rider's own POL-RD-02 figure (recomputed fare 24.82 on the booked optimal, refund 4.86, payable 4.90) is correct arithmetic but does not run once the deviation is exonerated; the fare ledger's closure block, which the rider says presupposes exoneration, is the block that governs. On the remaining points: POL-RD-06 gives no uplift and no conduct referral — the excess (4.5 km, 25.0%) is below both the 8.0 km and 50% materiality lines, and the only fields that clause may use (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 399) show no pattern; POL-RD-09 produces nothing, as there are no ERP or toll lines (0.00) and no airport surcharge, and where a deviation is exonerated POL-RD-09(2) leaves the distance and time charges standing; there is no rider instruction (POL-RD-04), no amended endpoint (POL-RD-05), no pooled itinerary (POL-RD-12, vehicle RYDE_X), and the fare is METERED, not upfront (POL-RD-11). The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), so the deviation stands on it and no corroboration or escalation under POL-RD-10(3) arises; I find none of POL-RD-10's other triggers either, so the case is ruled on rather than escalated. Every artifact this ruling rests on carries weight 1.0, and none is impaired or discounted. Outcome: NO_ACTION — payment_status remains CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd remains 0.00. The monetary effect is nil, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold. This ruling is provisional and may be appealed once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The charge stands; the outcome is NO_ACTION. The distance and time lines are left in place not because the measurement failed, but because the deviation is exonerated under POL-RD-03.\n\nThe deviation is real, and I accept the rider's measurement in full. The GPS trace EV-GPS-02808 records 22.5 km against a booked optimal of 18.0 km — an excess of 4.5 km, 25.00% — on a trace that is clean under POL-RD-07 (177 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s). Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%), and the trace figure governs over the rounded trip-record copy.\n\nPOL-RD-03 nonetheless exonerates the deviation. EV-ADVIS-02808-01 (weight 1.0, LTA DataMall) is a HIGH-severity multi-vehicle accident blocking 2 of 3 lanes on the PIE towards Tuas after the Eunos Link exit, active 06:09:18–07:33:38 — a 59.3-minute overlap with this 06:39:18–07:08:38 trip. Limb (a): the artifact records the advisory as intersecting the route, so the named segment is on the trip's planned path. Limb (b): the window covers the trip with far more than the 15-minute buffer at each end. Limb (c): the trace's own geometry check finds 0 fixes inside the advisory area and a minimum approach of 1,203 m, so the route actually driven did not pass through the affected segment — it left the corridor the optimal route takes and reached the drop-off after it. The rider's two POL-RD-03 objections are rejected: never coming within 1.2 km of an incident is what avoiding it looks like, not evidence against avoidance; and limb (a) rests on the advisory artifact's own recorded intersects-route finding, not on the absent optimal polyline. The rider's further point that the trace (22.5 km) is 1.5 km longer than the shortest lawful alternative (21.0 km) is met by the clause's own cap.\n\nThe cap: justified excess = min(4.5, 1.30 x (21.0 - 18.0) + 1.00 = 4.90) = 4.5 km — the whole of the measured excess. The closure-adjusted optimal is 18.0 + 4.5 = 22.5 km at 24.0 x (22.5 / 18.0) = 30.0 minutes. POL-RD-02, which the clause requires to be run against the adjusted route where an adjustment applies, gives ((3.80 + 0.75 x 22.5 + 0.28 x 30.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 29.8750, against charged_total 29.68; the refund is floored at zero, so nothing is payable. The rider's booked-optimal figures (recomputed fare 24.8200, refund 4.8600, rounded up to 4.90) are rejected as the arithmetic of a deviation that is not exonerated, as is the suggestion that the fare artifact's closure block 'presupposes' an exoneration the trace denies — the block simply applies the clause to the adjusted route.\n\nNo uplift and no referral follow. The 4.5 km / 25.00% excess is below both materiality limbs (8.0 km and 50%), and even if POL-RD-06 were consulted, the driver's trailing-window figures (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 399) establish no pattern, so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arise. On the fare ledger there are no ERP lines and no airport surcharge (the trip neither originates at an airport nor is billed one), so POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct, and under POL-RD-09(2) the distance and time charges stand on an external-cause exoneration while there is no off-route ERP to refund. POL-RD-04 (the one chat message is the driver's, not a rider instruction, and waypoint_hint is null), POL-RD-05 (pickup and dropoff were not amended), POL-RD-11 (METERED, quoted_fare_sgd null) and POL-RD-12 (RYDE_X, not a pooled trip) do not apply. No context-only profile field was used as a ground against either party; the referee's flag on the word 'rating' concerns a claim that expressly disclaims reliance on it, and it was given no weight.\n\nNo escalation: the trip identifiers match across the three instruments, the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing or window-mismatched artifact, and there is no mutually contradictory evidence of comparable strength — this is a question of applying POL-RD-03, which I have decided. The monetary effect is nil and does not exceed the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold. This ruling was made without human review and is provisional; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
